this environment provides none of them."], "uncertainties": ["Exact parameter name, default value, and semantics of the period setting in the real implementation; the two readings may collapse into one parameter or behave differently than modeled.", "Unstated compute budget; the full 84-run grid may need the Section 5 CPU-only fallback, which weakens statistical inference to a descriptive screen.", "Whether 3 seeds suffice for the Wilcoxon paired test; more seeds would strengthen claims.", "Possible interaction between period setting and lookback length, only partially addressed by the optional seq_len sensitivity check.", "Determinism of the FFT period-selection step (tie-breaking/numerical variance could add run-to-run noise beyond the seed effect)."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-211ec27c33cb47f3af044a61fd5e91b4", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-211ec27c33cb47f3af044a61fd5e91b4", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"answer": "FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN \u2014 \"How do different period settings affect the performance of the PDF model on the ETTm1 dataset?\" (Design-only; no experiment executed, no results claimed.)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. OBJECTIVE AND CORE INTERPRETATION (ASSUMPTION, NOT FACT)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nThe workspace contains no PDF source code (verified: only task.json in /workspace; no *.py, no configs, no ETTm1 CSV). \"PDF\" is therefore identified from published literature as the Periodicity Decoupling Framework for long-term forecasting, which uses an FFT step to extract dominant periods from the lookback window and decouples periodic from non-periodic components. Because the exact hyperparameter cannot be verified, the design treats \"period setting\" under TWO SEPARATE, EXPLICITLY ASSUMED readings:\n\n- Reading A \u2014 top-k retained periods: the model keeps the k most dominant FFT periods from the lookback window. Varied factor: k \u2208 {1, 2, 3, 5}. Default assumed k=1 unless literature says otherwise.\n- Reading B \u2014 period-selection mode: how the period(s) are chosen. Levels: (B1) learned/FFT top-k selection (model default), (B2) fixed 96-step daily period (matches ETTm1's 15-minute sampling), (B3) fixed 672-step weekly period.\n\nThese are two orthogonal one-factor experiments, not one merged sweep, so attribution stays clean. IF the researcher later supplies the actual PDF repository, Section 2's parameter names must be mapped to the real config arguments before execution; until then this mapping is an assumption.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n2. EXPERIMENTAL FACTORS AND CONTROLS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nIndependent variables (varied):\n- A-k: number of retained periods k \u2208 {1, 2, 3, 5}.\n- B-mode: selection mode \u2208 {FFT top-k, fixed 96, fixed 672}.\n- Horizon pred_len \u2208 {96, 192, 336, 720} \u2014 held as a within-design factor (not a control) because period effects plausibly interact with horizon; the two-way analysis (Section 4) requires it.\n\nFixed controls (identical across all cells, with rationale):\n1. Lookback seq_len = 96 (implementation default): the primary sweep must isolate the period setting; changing lookback would confound results because FFT period identification is lookback-sensitive. A separate sensitivity check (optional, Section 5) may add seq_len \u2208 {336, 512} on one horizon only.\n2. Dataset: ETTm1, all 7 channels, standard chronological 12-month train / 4-month val / 4-month test split. Rationale: this is the canonical ETT protocol; any other split breaks comparability with published baselines.\n3. Standardization: fit mean/std on the TRAIN portion only, applied to val/test. Rationale: fitting on val/test leaks information and inflates metrics.\n4. Seeds: 3 fixed seeds {1, 2, 3} shared across all configurations. Rationale: enables paired statistical tests on identical (data, init) conditions; \u22653 seeds give a usable std estimate at modest cost.\n5. Optimizer/schedule: Adam, learning rate from the model's published defaults for ETTm1 (assumed ~1e-4\u20131e-3 range, fixed once and reused for every cell). Rationale: per-cell LR tuning would mask period effects by absorbing them into optimization.\n6. Training budget: fixed maximum epochs with identical early-stopping patience (monitored on validation MSE). Rationale: early stopping on val MSE is the standard protocol and equalizes effective training effort.\n7. Batch size, loss (MSE), dropout/regularization, instance normalization if used by the model: all at implementation defaults, identical across cells.\n8. Data loader details (window stride, drop_last, shuffle=True on train only): identical across cells.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3. RUN PROTOCOL (NO EXECUTION PERFORMED)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nGrid: Reading A = 4 settings \u00d7 4 horizons \u00d7 3 seeds = 48 runs. Reading B = 3 modes \u00d7 4 horizons \u00d7 3 seeds = 36 runs. Total 84 runs (if the two readings share the same underlying parameter, run only the non-redundant union: k\u2208{1,2,3,5} under FFT mode plus fixed-96/fixed-672 at k=1 \u2192 6 settings \u00d7 4 \u00d7 3 = 72 runs).\nPer run: train on train split, select checkpoint by validation MSE, record test MSE and MAE, wall-clock training time, parameter count, and (diagnostic) the actual period(s) selected/resolved by the FFT step.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4. ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nPrimary outcome: test MSE (MAE secondary). \n- Descriptive: per-cell mean \u00b1 std over the 3 seeds, in a setting \u00d7 horizon table.\n- Two-way comparison: for each horizon, compare period settings pairwise using the Wilcoxon signed-rank test on paired seed-level MSEs (seeds shared across settings make pairs valid); additionally report the setting \u00d7 horizon interaction descriptively (does the best k change with horizon?). If a parametric route is preferred, a two-way repeated-measures ANOVA on log-MSE is an alternative, but the nonparametric test is primary given n=3 seeds.\n- Effect-size threshold: a difference is treated as meaningful only if the mean MSE gap exceeds 2% AND the paired test rejects at \u03b1=0.05 \u2014 prevents over-reading noise from 3 seeds.\n- Secondary outcomes: training time and parameter count per setting, to expose performance/cost trade-offs.\n- Optional diagnostic (strongly recommended): log which periods the FFT step selects per run and compare against ETTm1's known structure (96-step daily cycle; 672-step weekly cycle at 15-min sampling). This explains WHY a setting wins \u2014 e.g., whether top-2 selection captures {96, 672} \u2014 and turns the study into a mechanism check, not just a leaderboard.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n5. REDUCED CPU-ONLY FALLBACK PROTOCOL\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nCompute budget is unstated and GPU is disabled locally, so if only CPU is available: restrict to horizons {96, 720} (short and long extremes), the 3 most informative settings (k=1, k=3 or the best-per-dimension under Reading A; FFT vs fixed-96 under Reading B), and 1 seed each \u2192 6 runs. Analysis degrades to descriptive comparison only (no seed-paired test); this must be labeled as a preliminary screen, not the primary evidence. The full protocol above remains the design of record.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. FEASIBILITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n- Runtime estimate: PDF is an MLP-frequency hybrid, lightweight relative to Transformer baselines; a single ETTm1 run with early stopping is estimated at roughly 5\u201315 minutes on a single consumer GPU (order-of-magnitude, based on comparable MLP-based models \u2014 NOT measured here). Full 84-run grid \u2248 7\u201320 GPU-hours; trivially schedulable overnight on one GPU.\n- GPU assumption is EXTERNAL: this environment has gpu_enabled=false, network=disabled, no PyTorch, no ETTm1 data. Execution requires the researcher's own environment; the design only specifies what to run.\n- Data: ETT-small ETTm1.csv must be supplied externally (network is disabled here; acquisition is out of scope for this design).\n- Falsifiability (what would count as a meaningful, refutable answer \u2014 no results are claimed): H1 \u2014 k>1 (Reading A) improves test MSE over k=1, especially at long horizons, if multi-period structure exists in ETTm1; H2 \u2014 fixed 96-step mode \u2248 FFT top-1 (Reading B), because the daily cycle dominates ETTm1; a null result (all settings within the 2% + significance threshold) is itself a reportable finding that period settings are not performance-critical for PDF on ETTm1. Reversals of H1/H2 falsify the assumed mechanism. Every claim would be tied to the pre-specified table and test; nothing is post-hoc.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. ASSUMPTIONS (numbered \u2014 inferred, not verified)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. \"PDF\" = the published Periodicity Decoupling Framework model; no code exists in the workspace to confirm this.\n2. \"Period setting\" maps to a top-k retained-periods parameter and/or a selection-mode parameter as described in Section 1 \u2014 this is an ASSUMPTION about an unverifiable hyperparameter, not a fact.\n3. ETTm1 uses the standard chronological 12/4/4-month split with train-fitted standardization and horizons 96/192/336/720.\n4. PDF has published ETTm1 defaults for LR/batch/epochs that can be adopted as fixed controls.\n5. Execution compute (a GPU with ~8 GB+ memory) is available externally; nothing here can run locally (no data, no deps, no GPU, no network).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8. UNCERTAINTIES (numbered \u2014 open items)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. Exact parameter name, default, and semantics of the period setting in the real implementation; the two readings may collapse into one parameter or behave differently than modeled.\n2. Unstated compute budget; the full 84-run grid may need downscoping (Section 5 provides the fallback).\n3. Whether 3 seeds suffice for the paired test \u2014 acceptable for screening, borderline for strong claims; more seeds would strengthen inference.\n4. Whether period effects interact with lookback length (only partially addressed via the optional seq_len sensitivity check).\n5. Whether the FFT selection is deterministic (it should be, but ties/numerical issues in sorting frequencies could add run-to-run variance beyond the seed effect).\n\nDeliverable status: design only \u2014 nothing was run, no datasets were obtained, and no performance numbers exist or are implied.", "evidence": "Repository observations grounding the design: (1) /workspace contains exactly one file, task.json, which restates the question and includes track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" (2) grep for \"pdf\" in *.py and for \"ettm1\" recursively returns only task.json \u2014 no model code, configs, or scripts. (3) find for *.csv anywhere within depth 3 returns nothing \u2014 no ETTm1 data. (4) pip list shows no ML stack (no torch/pandas/numpy), confirming execution is impossible locally. (5) Environment flags: gpu_enabled=false, network=disabled, cpu_affinity_count=224. Design decisions therefore rest on the published PDF (Periodicity Decoupling Framework) architecture: FFT-based extraction of dominant periods, decoupling of periodic/non-periodic components, MLP backbone; ETTm1 at 15-min sampling has a natural 96-step daily and 672-step weekly cycle, motivating the fixed-period levels. All protocol choices (12/4/4 chronological split, train-only scaler, horizons 96\u2013720, val-MSE early stopping, shared seeds for paired testing) follow the standard long-term-forecasting evaluation convention used in the PDF paper's benchmark family.", "stage": "result", "assumptions": ["PDF refers to the published Periodicity Decoupling Framework model; no source code exists in the workspace to verify naming or defaults.", "The 'period setting' maps to a top-k retained-periods hyperparameter and/or a period-selection-mode hyperparameter (Section 1 readings A and B) \u2014 an assumption about an unverifiable parameter, not a fact.", "ETTm1 follows the canonical chronological 12/4/4-month split with train-set-only standardization and horizons 96/192/336/720.", "PDF has published ETTm1 defaults for learning rate, batch size, and epochs that serve as fixed controls.", "Any future execution requires externally supplied GPU compute, ETTm1 data, and dependencies; this environment provides none of them."], "uncertainties": ["Exact parameter name, default value, and semantics of the period setting in the real implementation; the two readings may collapse into one parameter or behave differently than modeled.", "Unstated compute budget; the full 84-run grid may need the Section 5 CPU-only fallback, which weakens statistical inference to a descriptive screen.", "Whether 3 seeds suffice for the Wilcoxon paired test; more seeds would strengthen claims.", "Possible interaction between period setting and lookback length, only partially addressed by the optional seq_len sensitivity check.", "Determinism of the FFT period-selection step (tie-breaking/numerical variance could add run-to-run noise beyond the seed effect)."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-fe5c3bde431f4e5f81a0017e0d5744d6", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {"answer": "FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN \u2014 \"How do different period settings affect the performance of the PDF model on the ETTm1 dataset?\" (Design-only; no experiment executed, no results claimed.)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. OBJECTIVE AND CORE INTERPRETATION (ASSUMPTION, NOT FACT)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nThe workspace contains no PDF source code (verified: only task.json in /workspace; no *.py, no configs, no ETTm1 CSV). \"PDF\" is therefore identified from published literature as the Periodicity Decoupling Framework for long-term forecasting, which uses an FFT step to extract dominant periods from the lookback window and decouples periodic from non-periodic components. Because the exact hyperparameter cannot be verified, the design treats \"period setting\" under TWO SEPARATE, EXPLICITLY ASSUMED readings:\n\n- Reading A \u2014 top-k retained periods: the model keeps the k most dominant FFT periods from the lookback window. Varied factor: k \u2208 {1, 2, 3, 5}. Default assumed k=1 unless literature says otherwise.\n- Reading B \u2014 period-selection mode: how the period(s) are chosen. Levels: (B1) learned/FFT top-k selection (model default), (B2) fixed 96-step daily period (matches ETTm1's 15-minute sampling), (B3) fixed 672-step weekly period.\n\nThese are two orthogonal one-factor experiments, not one merged sweep, so attribution stays clean. IF the researcher later supplies the actual PDF repository, Section 2's parameter names must be mapped to the real config arguments before execution; until then this mapping is an assumption.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n2. EXPERIMENTAL FACTORS AND CONTROLS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nIndependent variables (varied):\n- A-k: number of retained periods k \u2208 {1, 2, 3, 5}.\n- B-mode: selection mode \u2208 {FFT top-k, fixed 96, fixed 672}.\n- Horizon pred_len \u2208 {96, 192, 336, 720} \u2014 held as a within-design factor (not a control) because period effects plausibly interact with horizon; the two-way analysis (Section 4) requires it.\n\nFixed controls (identical across all cells, with rationale):\n1. Lookback seq_len = 96 (implementation default): the primary sweep must isolate the period setting; changing lookback would confound results because FFT period identification is lookback-sensitive. A separate sensitivity check (optional, Section 5) may add seq_len \u2208 {336, 512} on one horizon only.\n2. Dataset: ETTm1, all 7 channels, standard chronological 12-month train / 4-month val / 4-month test split. Rationale: this is the canonical ETT protocol; any other split breaks comparability with published baselines.\n3. Standardization: fit mean/std on the TRAIN portion only, applied to val/test. Rationale: fitting on val/test leaks information and inflates metrics.\n4. Seeds: 3 fixed seeds {1, 2, 3} shared across all configurations. Rationale: enables paired statistical tests on identical (data, init) conditions; \u22653 seeds give a usable std estimate at modest cost.\n5. Optimizer/schedule: Adam, learning rate from the model's published defaults for ETTm1 (assumed ~1e-4\u20131e-3 range, fixed once and reused for every cell). Rationale: per-cell LR tuning would mask period effects by absorbing them into optimization.\n6. Training budget: fixed maximum epochs with identical early-stopping patience (monitored on validation MSE). Rationale: early stopping on val MSE is the standard protocol and equalizes effective training effort.\n7. Batch size, loss (MSE), dropout/regularization, instance normalization if used by the model: all at implementation defaults, identical across cells.\n8. Data loader details (window stride, drop_last, shuffle=True on train only): identical across cells.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n3. RUN PROTOCOL (NO EXECUTION PERFORMED)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nGrid: Reading A = 4 settings \u00d7 4 horizons \u00d7 3 seeds = 48 runs. Reading B = 3 modes \u00d7 4 horizons \u00d7 3 seeds = 36 runs. Total 84 runs (if the two readings share the same underlying parameter, run only the non-redundant union: k\u2208{1,2,3,5} under FFT mode plus fixed-96/fixed-672 at k=1 \u2192 6 settings \u00d7 4 \u00d7 3 = 72 runs).\nPer run: train on train split, select checkpoint by validation MSE, record test MSE and MAE, wall-clock training time, parameter count, and (diagnostic) the actual period(s) selected/resolved by the FFT step.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n4. ANALYSIS PLAN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nPrimary outcome: test MSE (MAE secondary). \n- Descriptive: per-cell mean \u00b1 std over the 3 seeds, in a setting \u00d7 horizon table.\n- Two-way comparison: for each horizon, compare period settings pairwise using the Wilcoxon signed-rank test on paired seed-level MSEs (seeds shared across settings make pairs valid); additionally report the setting \u00d7 horizon interaction descriptively (does the best k change with horizon?). If a parametric route is preferred, a two-way repeated-measures ANOVA on log-MSE is an alternative, but the nonparametric test is primary given n=3 seeds.\n- Effect-size threshold: a difference is treated as meaningful only if the mean MSE gap exceeds 2% AND the paired test rejects at \u03b1=0.05 \u2014 prevents over-reading noise from 3 seeds.\n- Secondary outcomes: training time and parameter count per setting, to expose performance/cost trade-offs.\n- Optional diagnostic (strongly recommended): log which periods the FFT step selects per run and compare against ETTm1's known structure (96-step daily cycle; 672-step weekly cycle at 15-min sampling). This explains WHY a setting wins \u2014 e.g., whether top-2 selection captures {96, 672} \u2014 and turns the study into a mechanism check, not just a leaderboard.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n5. REDUCED CPU-ONLY FALLBACK PROTOCOL\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nCompute budget is unstated and GPU is disabled locally, so if only CPU is available: restrict to horizons {96, 720} (short and long extremes), the 3 most informative settings (k=1, k=3 or the best-per-dimension under Reading A; FFT vs fixed-96 under Reading B), and 1 seed each \u2192 6 runs. Analysis degrades to descriptive comparison only (no seed-paired test); this must be labeled as a preliminary screen, not the primary evidence. The full protocol above remains the design of record.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n6. FEASIBILITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n- Runtime estimate: PDF is an MLP-frequency hybrid, lightweight relative to Transformer baselines; a single ETTm1 run with early stopping is estimated at roughly 5\u201315 minutes on a single consumer GPU (order-of-magnitude, based on comparable MLP-based models \u2014 NOT measured here). Full 84-run grid \u2248 7\u201320 GPU-hours; trivially schedulable overnight on one GPU.\n- GPU assumption is EXTERNAL: this environment has gpu_enabled=false, network=disabled, no PyTorch, no ETTm1 data. Execution requires the researcher's own environment; the design only specifies what to run.\n- Data: ETT-small ETTm1.csv must be supplied externally (network is disabled here; acquisition is out of scope for this design).\n- Falsifiability (what would count as a meaningful, refutable answer \u2014 no results are claimed): H1 \u2014 k>1 (Reading A) improves test MSE over k=1, especially at long horizons, if multi-period structure exists in ETTm1; H2 \u2014 fixed 96-step mode \u2248 FFT top-1 (Reading B), because the daily cycle dominates ETTm1; a null result (all settings within the 2% + significance threshold) is itself a reportable finding that period settings are not performance-critical for PDF on ETTm1. Reversals of H1/H2 falsify the assumed mechanism. Every claim would be tied to the pre-specified table and test; nothing is post-hoc.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n7. ASSUMPTIONS (numbered \u2014 inferred, not verified)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. \"PDF\" = the published Periodicity Decoupling Framework model; no code exists in the workspace to confirm this.\n2. \"Period setting\" maps to a top-k retained-periods parameter and/or a selection-mode parameter as described in Section 1 \u2014 this is an ASSUMPTION about an unverifiable hyperparameter, not a fact.\n3. ETTm1 uses the standard chronological 12/4/4-month split with train-fitted standardization and horizons 96/192/336/720.\n4. PDF has published ETTm1 defaults for LR/batch/epochs that can be adopted as fixed controls.\n5. Execution compute (a GPU with ~8 GB+ memory) is available externally; nothing here can run locally (no data, no deps, no GPU, no network).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n8. UNCERTAINTIES (numbered \u2014 open items)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. Exact parameter name, default, and semantics of the period setting in the real implementation; the two readings may collapse into one parameter or behave differently than modeled.\n2. Unstated compute budget; the full 84-run grid may need downscoping (Section 5 provides the fallback).\n3. Whether 3 seeds suffice for the paired test \u2014 acceptable for screening, borderline for strong claims; more seeds would strengthen inference.\n4. Whether period effects interact with lookback length (only partially addressed via the optional seq_len sensitivity check).\n5. Whether the FFT selection is deterministic (it should be, but ties/numerical issues in sorting frequencies could add run-to-run variance beyond the seed effect).\n\nDeliverable status: design only \u2014 nothing was run, no datasets were obtained, and no performance numbers exist or are implied.", "evidence": "Repository observations grounding the design: (1) /workspace contains exactly one file, task.json, which restates the question and includes track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" (2) grep for \"pdf\" in *.py and for \"ettm1\" recursively returns only task.json \u2014 no model code, configs, or scripts. (3) find for *.csv anywhere within depth 3 returns nothing \u2014 no ETTm1 data. (4) pip list shows no ML stack (no torch/pandas/numpy), confirming execution is impossible locally. (5) Environment flags: gpu_enabled=false, network=disabled, cpu_affinity_count=224. Design decisions therefore rest on the published PDF (Periodicity Decoupling Framework) architecture: FFT-based extraction of dominant periods, decoupling of periodic/non-periodic components, MLP backbone; ETTm1 at 15-min sampling has a natural 96-step daily and 672-step weekly cycle, motivating the fixed-period levels. All protocol choices (12/4/4 chronological split, train-only scaler, horizons 96\u2013720, val-MSE early stopping, shared seeds for paired testing) follow the standard long-term-forecasting evaluation convention used in the PDF paper's benchmark family.", "stage": "result", "assumptions": ["PDF refers to the published Periodicity Decoupling Framework model; no source code exists in the workspace to verify naming or defaults.", "The 'period setting' maps to a top-k retained-periods hyperparameter and/or a period-selection-mode hyperparameter (Section 1 readings A and B) \u2014 an assumption about an unverifiable parameter, not a fact.", "ETTm1 follows the canonical chronological 12/4/4-month split with train-set-only standardization and horizons 96/192/336/720.", "PDF has published ETTm1 defaults for learning rate, batch size, and epochs that serve as fixed controls.", "Any future execution requires externally supplied GPU compute, ETTm1 data, and dependencies; this environment provides none of them."], "uncertainties": ["Exact parameter name, default value, and semantics of the period setting in the real implementation; the two readings may collapse into one parameter or behave differently than modeled.", "Unstated compute budget; the full 84-run grid may need the Section 5 CPU-only fallback, which weakens statistical inference to a descriptive screen.", "Whether 3 seeds suffice for the Wilcoxon paired test; more seeds would strengthen claims.", "Possible interaction between period setting and lookback length, only partially addressed by the optional seq_len sensitivity check.", "Determinism of the FFT period-selection step (tie-breaking/numerical variance could add run-to-run noise beyond the seed effect)."]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
